{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531714-all-editions-disagreements-about-nature-of-the-universe-among-the-changing-breeds","id":1531714,"title":"[All Editions] Disagreements about nature of the universe among the Changing Breeds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-28T18:19:43-08:00","id":1531714,"title":"[All Editions] Disagreements about nature of the universe among the Changing Breeds?","content":"Hi guys. I just wanted to confirm something.<br /> amon all versions of wta, the idea that Gaea is Supreme Being of All and everything else including the Triat comes below her is not a idea universally agreed upon by everyone in the setting,right?<br /> iirc other ideas include<ul><li>Gaea s very powerful, but the Triat is still more powerful than her</li> <li>Gaea is &quot;just&quot; an Incarna</li> <li>Gaea and the Triat are equals</li> <li>Gaea was created by an even more powerful being such as Coyote</li> </ul>all of those possibilities were brought upon in-setting,right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T22:35:10-08:00","id":1531724,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Nicolas Milioni;n1531714]Hi guys. I just wanted to confirm something.<br /> amon all versions of wta, the idea that Gaea is Supreme Being of All and everything else including the Triat comes below her is not a idea universally agreed upon by everyone in the setting,right?<br /> iirc other ideas include<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaea s very powerful, but the Triat is still more powerful than her </div> </div> </div>The most common alternative. Still doesn't get much air post-2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaea is &quot;just&quot; an Incarna </div> </div> </div>That's never been floated by the books; 1e never ranked her lower than Celestine. This seems to be a bit of garbled fanon that relies heavily on the existence of Eshtarra while also ignoring that Eshtarra exists as part of the whole of a much bigger spiritual being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaea and the Triat are equals </div> </div> </div>Rare to see, and I don't know if it's actually been done. It's usually either one is over or under the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaea was created by an even more powerful being such as Coyote </div> </div> </div>Always be careful when listening to Coyotes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> all of those possibilities were brought upon in-setting,right? </div> </div> </div>I've outlined which ones were and which weren't. Note that Bastet is actually the most gonzo in rejecting W:tA (it was basically a Mage crossover extravaganza), but it doesn't really offer an alternative as such. All the Fera books after that tended to whip sharply back the other way, and by Revised, most of the alternatives were rejected in favor of telling a coherent story about the Apocalypse (though also kept in the back of Apocalypse as optional flourishes on the book's four scenarios).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T05:00:46-08:00","id":1531728,"title":"","content":"Yeah, especially between different breeds of Shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> Ask Rokea, for example, you will get a wildlt different answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T06:55:30-08:00","id":1531734,"title":"","content":"Thanks folx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T13:14:17-08:00","id":1531798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531714-all-editions-disagreements-about-nature-of-the-universe-among-the-changing-breeds#post1531714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys. I just wanted to confirm something.<br /> amon all versions of wta, the idea that Gaea is Supreme Being of All and everything else including the Triat comes below her is not a idea universally agreed upon by everyone in the setting,right?<br /> iirc other ideas include<ul><li>Gaea s very powerful, but the Triat is still more powerful than her</li> <li>Gaea is &quot;just&quot; an Incarna</li> <li>Gaea and the Triat are equals</li> <li>Gaea was created by an even more powerful being such as Coyote</li> </ul>all of those possibilities were brought upon in-setting,right?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Dino has ran them down, I'm not gonna go along this in detail, but in general, the tales of the Coyotes and the Cats are the least credible when looking at all of them together. Which doesn't mean that they couldn't be true at your table.<br /> <br /> The biggest question usually is: &quot;Is Gaia more powerful or the Triat&quot;, and this is one that's a huge theological thing for quite a few different Shifters and over which somebody will get killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T18:47:40-08:00","id":1531833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531714-all-editions-disagreements-about-nature-of-the-universe-among-the-changing-breeds?p=1531798#post1531798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Dino has ran them down, I'm not gonna go along this in detail, but in general, the tales of the Coyotes and the Cats are the least credible when looking at all of them together. Which doesn't mean that they couldn't be true at your table.<br /> <br /> The biggest question usually is: &quot;Is Gaia more powerful or the Triat&quot;, and this is one that's a huge theological thing for quite a few different Shifters and over which somebody will get killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cats and Coyotes could also have just gone for gonzo to hide secrets in their tales, while still being broadly disconnected from how everyone agrees it went down (the &quot;everyone&quot; here also including some powerful and long-lived spirits.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}